<%# Overall progress. Kept separate so a step landing does not re-render the whole page.

    `case` gets its own ERB tag and each `when` gets another. Squeezed into a single tag with inline
    `then` continuations it was unreadable, and Herb reports it as a parse error: a case with its
    conditions inside one tag cannot be reliably parsed, compiled or formatted.

    Careful in here: ERB comment delimiters do not nest, so writing a closing tag inside this text
    ends the comment early and the rest becomes markup. That is what broke this file once already. %>
<p class="status status--<%= analysis.status %>" id="analysis_status">
  <% case analysis.status %>
  <% when "pending" %>
    Queued…
  <% when "running" %>
    Running. Fast checks appear first; Common Crawl and the model probes take longer.
  <% when "done" %>
    Done<% if analysis.replayed? %>, replayed from cache<% end %>.
    <% if analysis.cost_millicents.positive? %>
      <small>Model spend: <%= (analysis.cost_millicents / 1000.0).round(3) %> dollars</small>
    <% end %>
  <% when "failed" %>
    Something failed. Partial results are shown below.
  <% end %>
</p>
